== A1. exponent E for every odd prime p < 4000 (explicit orbit decomposition on Z_(p^2) \ {0})
   p =     3: ord_p(2) = 2, d' = 1, ord_(p^2)(g) = 3, E = 2 (non-Wieferich value 2), Wieferich False
   p =     5: ord_p(2) = 4, d' = 1, ord_(p^2)(g) = 5, E = 4 (non-Wieferich value 4), Wieferich False
   p =     7: ord_p(2) = 3, d' = 3, ord_(p^2)(g) = 21, E = 2 (non-Wieferich value 2), Wieferich False
   p =    31: ord_p(2) = 5, d' = 5, ord_(p^2)(g) = 155, E = 6 (non-Wieferich value 6), Wieferich False
   p =   127: ord_p(2) = 7, d' = 7, ord_(p^2)(g) = 889, E = 18 (non-Wieferich value 18), Wieferich False
   p =  1093: ord_p(2) = 364, d' = 91, ord_(p^2)(g) = 91, E = 6564 (non-Wieferich value 12), Wieferich True
   p =  3511: ord_p(2) = 1755, d' = 1755, ord_(p^2)(g) = 1755, E = 3512 (non-Wieferich value 2), Wieferich True
   primes p < 4000 where E differs from (p-1)/d': [(1093, 6564, 12, True), (3511, 3512, 2, True)]
   anomalies (orbit closed under negation / odd N / formula mismatch / even order): []

== A2. brute force: g-invariant circulant tournaments on Z_n (all connection sets enumerated)
   Z_ 9, base 2: g = 2^2 = 4: ord_(p^2)(g) = 3, ord_p(g) = 1; invariant tournaments (brute force) = 4, orbit formula 2^(N/2) = 4;  match True;  0.1 s
   Z_25, base 2: g = 2^4 = 16: ord_(p^2)(g) = 5, ord_p(g) = 1; invariant tournaments (brute force) = 16, orbit formula 2^(N/2) = 16;  match True;  0.0 s
   Z_49, base 2: g = 2: ord_(p^2)(g) = 21, ord_p(g) = 3; invariant tournaments (brute force) = 4, orbit formula 2^(N/2) = 4;  match True;  0.2 s
