== A4. rigidity of circulant tournaments of prime order
   p =  3: brute-force |Aut| over all 2 circulant tournaments: {3: 2}
   p =  5: brute-force |Aut| over all 4 circulant tournaments: {5: 4}
   p =  7: brute-force |Aut| over all 8 circulant tournaments: {7: 6, 21: 2}
   p = 11: brute-force |Aut| over all 32 circulant tournaments: {11: 30, 55: 2}
   p = 13: brute-force |Aut| over all 64 circulant tournaments: {13: 60, 39: 4}
   p = 17: brute-force |Aut| over all 256 circulant tournaments: {17: 256}
   primes p <= 31 at which every circulant tournament has trivial multiplier stabilizer: [3, 5, 17]
   rotational classes at Fermat primes 2^((p-1)/2)/(p-1): {3: 1, 5: 1, 17: 16, 257: '2^120', 65537: '2^32752'}

